  "reasoning": "The claim has been denied twice for CO-97 (bundling) and a previous appeal with medical necessity was unsuccessful, indicating that standard appeal arguments are not overcoming the payer's bundling logic. Since the payer offers peer-to-peer review and the denial is still on the table, this is the most appropriate next step to challenge the medical director's decision on the separate payable status of CPT 93271. Escalation is not yet warranted as a specific, available action (P2P) can properly progress the claim.",
